# Guidelines

- Never overwrite manual edits I have made unless I explicitly ask you to. If
  such edits conflict with changes you are trying to make, consult me regarding
  how to proceed.
- Check whether an applicable skill or documented convention exists before
  improvising an approach.

## Environment

- I work one git worktree per task, managed by `wt` (worktrunk), laid out as
  `~/worktrees/{repo}.{branch}` (branch sanitized). Don't invent a different
  scheme.

## Scope of this file

Cross-cutting policy only. Project conventions belong in that project's
`AGENTS.md`. Language and workflow procedures belong in skills.

